(>> Solution to Question 1:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Define a Crystal Lattice, Basis, and Unit Cell. State the seven crystal systems in three dimensions along with their axial length and interaxial angle relationships.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Fundamental Crystallographic Definitions:) Tj
T*
(   - Space Lattice: An infinite three-dimensional periodic array of mathematical points in space) Tj
T*
(   in which every point possesses surroundings identical to every other point.) Tj
T*
(   - Basis \(Motif\): A group of one or more atoms, ions, or molecules having identical spatial) Tj
T*
(   configuration attached to each lattice point.) Tj
T*
(   - Fundamental Law of Crystallography: Crystal Structure = Space Lattice + Basis.) Tj
T*
(   - Unit Cell: The fundamental repeating geometric volumetric building block of a crystal lattice) Tj
T*
(   that reproduces the entire crystal through continuous translations along primitive vectors a,) Tj
T*
(   b, and c.) Tj
T*
(   - Primitive Cell: A minimal unit cell containing exactly ONE constituent lattice point \(e.g.,) Tj
T*
(   Wigner-Seitz cell\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The Seven Crystal Systems and Metric Tensor Relations:) Tj
T*
(   In 3D space, all crystalline geometries are categorized into 7 crystal systems defined by 6) Tj
T*
(   lattice parameters \(a, b, c, alpha, beta, gamma\):) Tj
T*
(   \(1\) Cubic System: a = b = c; alpha = beta = gamma = 90 deg. \(3 Bravais lattices: SC, BCC, FCC\).) Tj
T*
(   \(2\) Tetragonal System: a = b != c; alpha = beta = gamma = 90 deg. \(2 Bravais lattices: Simple,) Tj
T*
(   Body-Centered\).) Tj
T*
(   \(3\) Orthorhombic System: a != b != c; alpha = beta = gamma = 90 deg. \(4 Bravais lattices:) Tj
T*
(   Simple, Body-Centered, Base-Centered, Face-Centered\).) Tj
T*
(   \(4\) Rhombohedral \(Trigonal\) System: a = b = c; alpha = beta = gamma != 90 deg \(< 120 deg\). \(1) Tj
T*
(   Bravais lattice\).) Tj
T*
(   \(5\) Hexagonal System: a = b != c; alpha = beta = 90 deg, gamma = 120 deg. \(1 Bravais lattice\).) Tj
T*
(   \(6\) Monoclinic System: a != b != c; alpha = gamma = 90 deg, beta != 90 deg. \(2 Bravais) Tj
T*
(   lattices: Simple, Base-Centered\).) Tj
T*
(   \(7\) Triclinic System: a != b != c; alpha != beta != gamma != 90 deg \(Lowest possible crystal) Tj
T*
(   symmetry, 1 Bravais lattice\).) Tj
T*
(   Total Bravais Lattices in 3D space: 3 + 2 + 4 + 1 + 1 + 2 + 1 = 14 Bravais Lattices.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
