(>> Solution to Question 2:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the Atomic Packing Factor \(APF\), Coordination Number, effective number of atoms per unit cell, and atomic radius relation with lattice constant for Simple Cubic \(SC\), Body-Centered Cubic \(BCC\), and Face-Centered Cubic \(FCC\) crystal structures.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Simple Cubic \(SC\) Structure:) Tj
T*
(   - Atoms per cell: 8 corner atoms * \(1/8 share\) = 1 atom/cell.) Tj
T*
(   - Coordination Number \(CN\): Each atom has 6 nearest neighbors along +/- x, +/- y, +/- z => CN =) Tj
T*
(   6.) Tj
T*
(   - Nearest neighbor contact: Atoms touch along cell edges: 2*r = a => r = a / 2.) Tj
T*
(   - Atomic Packing Factor \(APF\):) Tj
T*
(   APF = \(N * Volume of 1 atom\) / \(Volume of unit cell\) = [ 1 * \(4/3\)*pi*r^3 ] / a^3 = [) Tj
T*
(   \(4/3\)*pi*\(a/2\)^3 ] / a^3 = pi / 6 = 0.5236 =~ 52.4%.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Body-Centered Cubic \(BCC\) Structure:) Tj
T*
(   - Atoms per cell: 8 corners * \(1/8\) + 1 central body atom * 1 = 2 atoms/cell.) Tj
T*
(   - Coordination Number \(CN\): Central atom touches all 8 corner atoms => CN = 8.) Tj
T*
(   - Nearest neighbor contact: Atoms touch along the body diagonal of length a*sqrt\(3\):) Tj
T*
(   4 * r = a * sqrt\(3\) => r = a * sqrt\(3\) / 4.) Tj
T*
ET

