(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the general expression for the theoretical density rho of a crystalline solid in terms of its lattice parameter 'a', effective number of atoms per unit cell N, atomic mass M, and Avogadro's number N_A. Calculate the density of Face-Centered Cubic Copper \(M = 63.54 g/mol, a = 0.3615 nm, N_A = 6.022 * 10^23 mol^-1\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Analytical Derivation of Density Formula:) Tj
T*
(   Let the unit cell be a cube of edge length 'a'.) Tj
T*
(   - Volume of unit cell: V_cell = a^3.) Tj
T*
(   - Number of atoms in unit cell = N.) Tj
T*
(   - Mass of a single atom: m_atom = M / N_A, where M is atomic molar mass \(in kg/mol or g/mol\)) Tj
T*
(   and N_A is Avogadro's constant.) Tj
T*
(   - Total mass inside unit cell: m_cell = N * \(M / N_A\).) Tj
T*
(   - Theoretical Density rho:) Tj
T*
(   rho = m_cell / V_cell = \( N * M \) / \( N_A * a^3 \).) Tj
T*
(   In standard SI units: [kg/m^3] = [ \(atoms\) * \(kg/mol\) ] / [ \(atoms/mol\) * \(m^3\) ].) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Numerical Evaluation for FCC Copper:) Tj
T*
(   - Structure: FCC => N = 4 atoms per unit cell.) Tj
T*
(   - Molar mass M = 63.54 g/mol = 63.54 * 10^-3 kg/mol.) Tj
T*
(   - Lattice constant a = 0.3615 nm = 0.3615 * 10^-9 m.) Tj
T*
(   - Unit cell volume a^3 = \(0.3615 * 10^-9\)^3 = 4.724 * 10^-29 m^3.) Tj
T*
(   - Avogadro constant N_A = 6.022 * 10^23 mol^-1.) Tj
T*
(   Substitute into density formula:) Tj
T*
(   rho = \( 4 * 63.54 * 10^-3 \) / [ \(6.022 * 10^23\) * \(4.724 * 10^-29\) ].) Tj
T*
(   rho = 0.25416 / [ 2.845 * 10^-5 ] = 8,933.6 kg/m^3 =~ 8.93 g/cm^3.) Tj
T*
(   Comparison with literature: The experimentally measured density of pure metallic copper is 8.94) Tj
T*
(   g/cm^3 \(less than 0.1% deviation\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
