(   - Step 3 \(Take Reciprocals\): Invert each intercept: 1/p, 1/q, 1/r. \(1/infinity = 0\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 4 \(Clear Fractions\): Multiply the reciprocals by their Least Common Denominator \(LCD\) to) Tj
T*
(   yield the smallest set of coprime integers: h, k, l.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 5 \(Format\): Enclose the integers in parentheses without commas: \(h k l\). If an intercept) Tj
T*
(   is negative, place a bar over the index: \(h bar-k l\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Derivation of Interplanar Spacing d_hkl in Cubic Lattices:) Tj
T*
(   Consider plane ABC belonging to family \(hkl\) closest to origin O.) Tj
T*
(   Intercepts on axes: OA = a/h, OB = a/k, OC = a/l.) Tj
T*
(   Let ON be the perpendicular normal drawn from origin O to plane ABC. The length ON = d_hkl.) Tj
T*
(   Let direction cosines of normal ON with axes x, y, z be cos\(alpha\), cos\(beta\), cos\(gamma\):) Tj
T*
(   cos\(alpha\) = d / OA = d / \(a/h\) = \(d * h\) / a.) Tj
T*
(   cos\(beta\) = d / OB = d / \(a/k\) = \(d * k\) / a.) Tj
T*
(   cos\(gamma\) = d / OC = d / \(a/l\) = \(d * l\) / a.) Tj
T*
(   By the fundamental trigonometric identity of direction cosines in orthogonal 3D space:) Tj
T*
(   cos^2\(alpha\) + cos^2\(beta\) + cos^2\(gamma\) = 1.) Tj
T*
(   [ \(d * h\) / a ]^2 + [ \(d * k\) / a ]^2 + [ \(d * l\) / a ]^2 = 1.) Tj
T*
(   \(d^2 / a^2\) * [ h^2 + k^2 + l^2 ] = 1.) Tj
T*
(   d^2 = a^2 / \(h^2 + k^2 + l^2\) => d_hkl = a / sqrt\( h^2 + k^2 + l^2 \).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
