(   [Problem Statement]: Monochromatic X-rays of wavelength lambda = 0.154 nm \(Cu-K_alpha radiation\) are incident on a cubic crystal of lattice parameter a = 0.408 nm \(Gold\). Calculate: \(1\) Interplanar spacings for \(1 1 1\), \(2 0 0\), and \(2 2 0\) planes, \(2\) First-order \(n = 1\) Bragg diffraction glancing angles theta for each plane.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Interplanar Spacing Calculations \(d_hkl = a / sqrt\(h^2 + k^2 + l^2\)\):) Tj
T*
(   Given a = 0.408 nm:) Tj
T*
(   - \(1 1 1\) plane: d_111 = 0.408 / sqrt\(1^2 + 1^2 + 1^2\) = 0.408 / sqrt\(3\) = 0.408 / 1.73205 =) Tj
T*
(   0.23556 nm = 0.2356 nm.) Tj
T*
(   - \(2 0 0\) plane: d_200 = 0.408 / sqrt\(2^2 + 0 + 0\) = 0.408 / 2 = 0.2040 nm.) Tj
T*
(   - \(2 2 0\) plane: d_220 = 0.408 / sqrt\(2^2 + 2^2 + 0\) = 0.408 / sqrt\(8\) = 0.408 / 2.8284 =) Tj
T*
(   0.14425 nm = 0.1443 nm.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. First-Order Bragg Glancing Angles \(sin\(theta\) = lambda / \(2 * d\)\):) Tj
T*
(   Given lambda = 0.154 nm, n = 1:) Tj
T*
(   - For \(1 1 1\) planes:) Tj
T*
(   sin\(theta_111\) = 0.154 / \(2 * 0.23556\) = 0.154 / 0.47112 = 0.32688.) Tj
T*
(   theta_111 = asin\(0.32688\) = 19.08 degrees.) Tj
T*
(   - For \(2 0 0\) planes:) Tj
T*
(   sin\(theta_200\) = 0.154 / \(2 * 0.2040\) = 0.154 / 0.4080 = 0.37745.) Tj
T*
(   theta_200 = asin\(0.37745\) = 22.17 degrees.) Tj
T*
(   - For \(2 2 0\) planes:) Tj
T*
(   sin\(theta_220\) = 0.154 / \(2 * 0.14425\) = 0.154 / 0.2885 = 0.53380.) Tj
T*
(   theta_220 = asin\(0.53380\) = 32.26 degrees.) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion: d_111 = 0.236 nm \(theta = 19.1 deg\); d_200 = 0.204 nm \(theta = 22.2 deg\); d_220 =) Tj
T*
(   0.144 nm \(theta = 32.3 deg\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
