BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 7:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Classify Crystal Imperfections \(Lattice Defects\) based on their dimensionality: Point defects, Line defects, Planar defects, and Volume defects. Explain Schottky and Frenkel defects with neat schematic representations.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Dimensional Classification of Crystal Imperfections:) Tj
T*
(   No real engineering crystal is perfectly periodic. Lattice defects strongly control yield) Tj
T*
(   strength, electrical resistivity, and diffusion.) Tj
T*
(   - 1. Zero-Dimensional \(Point Defects\): Localized atomic disruptions affecting 1-2 atomic sites.) Tj
T*
(   * Vacancy \(missing host atom\), Interstitial \(host or foreign atom squeezed into non-lattice) Tj
T*
(   void\), Substitutional impurity.) Tj
T*
(   - 2. One-Dimensional \(Line Defects / Dislocations\): Boundary lines separating slipped and) Tj
T*
(   unslipped regions of a crystal plane.) Tj
T*
(   * Edge Dislocation \(extra half-plane of atoms; Burgers vector perpendicular to dislocation) Tj
T*
(   line\).) Tj
T*
(   * Screw Dislocation \(helical ramp of atoms; Burgers vector parallel to dislocation line\).) Tj
T*
(   - 3. Two-Dimensional \(Planar / Interfacial Defects\): Internal boundaries separating regions of) Tj
T*
(   differing crystallographic orientation.) Tj
T*
