(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Band Theory of Solids based on the Kronig-Penney Model. Discuss how the periodic potential of a crystal splits atomic energy levels into allowed energy bands and forbidden band gaps.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Physical Basis of Band Formation:) Tj
T*
(   In an isolated atom, electron energy levels are discrete and sharp. When N atoms assemble into) Tj
T*
(   a crystal lattice,) Tj
T*
(   their outer valence electron wave functions overlap. According to the Pauli exclusion) Tj
T*
(   principle, no two electrons can occupy) Tj
T*
(   identical quantum states. Consequently, each discrete atomic energy level splits into N closely) Tj
T*
(   spaced quasi-continuous levels,) Tj
T*
(   forming continuous Allowed Energy Bands separated by Forbidden Energy Gaps \(Band Gaps E_g\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Kronig-Penney Model Formulation:) Tj
T*
(   Kronig and Penney \(1931\) modeled the 1D periodic crystal potential as an infinite array of) Tj
T*
(   rectangular potential wells and barriers:) Tj
T*
(   V\(x\) = 0 for 0 < x < a \(well of width a\); V\(x\) = V0 for -b < x < 0 \(barrier of height V0 and) Tj
T*
(   width b\).) Tj
T*
