(   [Problem Statement]: Distinguish between Conductors, Semiconductors, and Insulators on the basis of Band Theory. Draw representative energy band diagrams illustrating the conduction band, valence band, and forbidden band gap for each category.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Conductors \(Metals, e.g., Cu, Al, Na\):) Tj
T*
(   - Band Architecture: The valence band overlaps with the conduction band, or the conduction band) Tj
T*
(   is partially filled at 0 K.) Tj
T*
(   - Forbidden Gap: E_g = 0 eV \(No forbidden gap\).) Tj
T*
(   - Electronic Behavior: Abundant empty energy states exist immediately adjacent to filled) Tj
T*
(   states. Even an infinitesimal applied electric field accelerates electrons into higher states,) Tj
T*
(   producing immense electrical conductivity \(sigma ~ 10^7 S/m\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Semiconductors \(e.g., Silicon E_g = 1.1 eV, Germanium E_g = 0.67 eV, GaAs E_g = 1.42 eV\):) Tj
T*
(   - Band Architecture: Completely filled valence band and completely empty conduction band at T =) Tj
T*
(   0 K.) Tj
T*
(   - Forbidden Gap: Narrow energy band gap: 0.1 eV < E_g < 2.0 eV \(typically ~ 1 eV\).) Tj
T*
(   - Electronic Behavior: At 0 K, behaves as a perfect insulator. At room temperature \(~300 K\),) Tj
T*
(   thermal energy k_B*T \(~0.026 eV\) excites a finite concentration of electrons across the narrow) Tj
T*
(   gap into the conduction band, leaving equal mobile holes in the valence band \(conductivity) Tj
T*
(   sigma ~ 10^-3 to 10^2 S/m\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Insulators \(e.g., Diamond E_g = 5.4 eV, Quartz SiO2 E_g ~ 9 eV\):) Tj
T*
(   - Band Architecture: Completely filled valence band and completely empty conduction band.) Tj
T*
(   - Forbidden Gap: Extremely wide band gap: E_g > 3 to 5 eV.) Tj
T*
(   - Electronic Behavior: Thermal energy at room temperature is vastly insufficient to promote) Tj
T*
(   electrons across the huge forbidden gap. Electrical conductivity is negligible \(sigma < 10^-12) Tj
T*
(   S/m\), with immense dielectric breakdown strength.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
