(   From quantum relation E = h_bar * omega => omega = E / h_bar:) Tj
T*
(   v_g = \(1 / h_bar\) * \(dE / dk\). \(Equation 1\)) Tj
T*
(   Now apply an external electric field E. The external work done on the electron in time dt) Tj
T*
(   produces energy change dE:) Tj
T*
(   dE = F * dx = F * v_g * dt => dE / dt = F * v_g.) Tj
T*
(   Also, by chain rule: dE / dt = \(dE / dk\) * \(dk / dt\) = \(h_bar * v_g\) * \(dk / dt\).) Tj
T*
(   Equating both expressions: F * v_g = h_bar * v_g * \(dk / dt\) => h_bar * \(dk / dt\) = F.) Tj
T*
(   \(Equation 2\)) Tj
T*
(   Now differentiate group velocity \(Equation 1\) with respect to time to obtain acceleration a:) Tj
T*
(   a = dv_g / dt = \(1 / h_bar\) * d/dt\( dE / dk \) = \(1 / h_bar\) * \(d^2E / dk^2\) * \(dk / dt\).) Tj
T*
(   Substitute dk/dt = F / h_bar from Equation 2:) Tj
T*
(   a = \(1 / h_bar\) * \(d^2E / dk^2\) * \(F / h_bar\) = [ \(1 / h_bar^2\) * \(d^2E / dk^2\) ] * F.) Tj
T*
(   Comparing with Newton's Second Law a = F / m*:) Tj
T*
(   1 / m* = \(1 / h_bar^2\) * \( d^2E / dk^2 \) => m* = h_bar^2 / \( d^2E / dk^2 \).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Physical Interpretation:) Tj
T*
(   - Bottom of Band \(d^2E/dk^2 > 0\): Curvature is concave upward => m* > 0. Electron accelerates) Tj
T*
(   in direction of applied electric force.) Tj
T*
(   - Top of Band \(d^2E/dk^2 < 0\): Curvature is concave downward => m* < 0. Electron accelerates) Tj
T*
(   OPPOSITE to applied force due to intense Bragg reflection from the periodic lattice. A state) Tj
T*
(   with negative effective mass electron is physically equivalent to a positive charge carrier) Tj
T*
(   \(Hole\).) Tj
T*
(   - Inflection Point \(d^2E/dk^2 = 0\): m* approaches infinity. Electron cannot be accelerated by) Tj
T*
(   external fields.) Tj
