(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Hall Effect in semiconductors. Derive the expressions for Hall Voltage V_H, Hall Coefficient R_H, and carrier concentration 'n'. Explain how Hall effect measurements distinguish between n-type and p-type semiconductors.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Physical Principle:) Tj
T*
(   When a current-carrying semiconductor strip is placed in a transverse magnetic field B, the) Tj
T*
(   charge carriers experience a transverse Lorentz force) Tj
T*
(   perpendicular to both current and magnetic field vectors: F_B = q * \(v_d x B\).) Tj
T*
(   This deflects carriers toward one lateral edge, building up surface charge and creating a) Tj
T*
(   transverse electric field E_H \(Hall Field\)) Tj
T*
(   until the electrostatic force exactly balances the magnetic Lorentz force:) Tj
T*
(   F_E + F_B = 0 => q * E_H = q * v_d * B => E_H = v_d * B.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Derivation of Hall Coefficient and Voltage:) Tj
T*
(   Let strip have width w, thickness t, carrying current I along x-axis, with magnetic field B) Tj
T*
(   along z-axis.) Tj
T*
(   - Current density: J = I / \(w * t\) = n * q * v_d => v_d = J / \(n * q\).) Tj
T*
(   - Hall Electric Field: E_H = v_d * B = \( J * B \) / \( n * q \).) Tj
T*
(   - Hall Voltage across width w: V_H = E_H * w = \( J * B * w \) / \( n * q \) = [ \(I / \(w*t\)\) * B *) Tj
T*
(   w ] / \( n * q \) = \( I * B \) / \( n * q * t \).) Tj
T*
(   - Hall Coefficient R_H is defined as: R_H = E_H / \( J * B \) = 1 / \( n * q \).) Tj
T*
(   - Therefore: V_H = \( R_H * I * B \) / t.) Tj
T*
(   - Carrier Concentration: n = 1 / \( |R_H| * e \).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Identification of Semiconductor Type:) Tj
T*
(   - For n-type semiconductor: Charge carriers are electrons \(q = - e\) => R_H = - 1 / \(n * e\) < 0) Tj
T*
(   \(Hall coefficient is NEGATIVE\).) Tj
T*
(   - For p-type semiconductor: Charge carriers are holes \(q = + e\) => R_H = + 1 / \(p * e\) > 0) Tj
T*
ET

