(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the BCS Theory of Superconductivity. Describe the formation of Cooper Pairs via electron-phonon-electron interactions and explain how energy gap Delta\(T\) accounts for zero resistivity.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Microscopic Mechanism \(Bardeen, Cooper, and Schrieffer, 1957\):) Tj
T*
(   BCS theory demonstrates that conventional superconductivity is driven by an effective) Tj
T*
(   attractive interaction between pairs of conduction electrons) Tj
T*
(   mediated by virtual acoustic lattice vibrations \(phonons\):) Tj
T*
(   - An electron passing through the lattice exerts Coulomb attraction on positive ion cores,) Tj
T*
(   pulling them inward and creating a localized region of concentrated positive charge \(lattice) Tj
T*
(   polarization / virtual phonon emission\).) Tj
T*
(   - Because heavy ions move slowly \(plasma frequency << electron speed\), the positive charge peak) Tj
T*
(   persists after the first electron has departed.) Tj
T*
(   - A second electron trailing behind is attracted to this lingering positive region \(virtual) Tj
T*
(   phonon absorption\).) Tj
T*
(   - This net attractive interaction overcomes direct screened Coulomb repulsion for electrons) Tj
T*
(   near the Fermi surface with equal and opposite momenta and antiparallel spins: \(k, up\) and \(-k,) Tj
T*
(   down\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Formation of Cooper Pairs:) Tj
T*
(   This bound pair of two electrons is termed a Cooper Pair. Because each electron has spin 1/2, a) Tj
T*
(   Cooper pair has integer total spin \(S = 1/2 - 1/2 = 0\),) Tj
T*
(   behaving collectively as a Composite Boson.) Tj
T*
(   Below T_c, millions of Cooper pairs condense into a single coherent, macroscopic ground quantum) Tj
T*
(   state spanning the entire crystal.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Superconducting Energy Gap Delta\(T\):) Tj
T*
(   - The condensation of Cooper pairs lowers the system ground energy, opening a forbidden energy) Tj
T*
(   gap 2*Delta\(T\) centered at the Fermi level.) Tj
T*
(   - At T = 0 K, BCS theory predicts: 2 * Delta\(0\) = 3.52 * k_B * T_c.) Tj
T*
(   - To scatter a Cooper pair and produce electrical resistance, a collision must supply energy) Tj
T*
(   greater than 2*Delta to break the pair into normal quasi-particles.) Tj
T*
ET

