(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the concept of Magnetic Flux Quantization in a superconducting ring. Derive the expression for the Magnetic Flux Quantum Phi_0 = h / \(2*e\) and state its numerical value.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Physical Background:) Tj
T*
(   Consider a hollow superconducting cylinder or ring cooled below T_c in an external magnetic) Tj
T*
(   field.) Tj
T*
(   When the field is turned off, persistent supercurrents circulate around the inner perimeter to) Tj
T*
(   trap magnetic flux inside the hole.) Tj
T*
(   Because the macroscopic superconducting wave function Psi\(r\) = sqrt\(n_s\) * e^\(i * theta\(r\)\)) Tj
T*
(   must be single-valued around any closed loop C,) Tj
T*
(   the total magnetic flux Phi trapped within the ring cannot take arbitrary values, but is) Tj
T*
(   strictly quantized in integer multiples of a fundamental flux quantum Phi_0.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Derivation of Flux Quantum Phi_0:) Tj
T*
(   The canonical momentum of a Cooper pair of mass 2*m and charge q = - 2*e in magnetic vector) Tj
T*
(   potential A is:) Tj
T*
(   p = 2*m*v + q*A = h_bar * Grad\(theta\).) Tj
T*
(   Deep inside the superconductor bulk \(beyond London penetration depth lambda_L\), supercurrent) Tj
T*
(   density J = 0 => v = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Therefore: q * A = h_bar * Grad\(theta\) => A = \( h_bar / q \) * Grad\(theta\).) Tj
T*
(   Integrate along a closed path C encircling the hollow interior:) Tj
T*
(   Closed_Integral A dot dl = \( h_bar / q \) * Closed_Integral Grad\(theta\) dot dl.) Tj
T*
(   By Stokes' Theorem, the line integral of A is the total enclosed magnetic flux Phi:) Tj
T*
(   Closed_Integral A dot dl = Surface_Integral \(Curl A\) dot dS = Surface_Integral B dot dS = Phi.) Tj
T*
(   For wave function single-valuedness, the phase change around the closed loop must be an integer) Tj
T*
(   multiple of 2*pi:) Tj
T*
(   Closed_Integral Grad\(theta\) dot dl = Delta theta = n * 2*pi \(where n = 0, 1, 2, ...\).) Tj
T*
(   Therefore: Phi = \( h_bar / q \) * \( n * 2*pi \) = \( h / \(2*pi*q\) \) * 2*pi*n = n * \( h / q \).) Tj
T*
(   Substituting Cooper pair charge q = 2*e:) Tj
T*
(   Phi = n * [ h / \(2 * e\) ] = n * Phi_0.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Fundamental Flux Quantum Value:) Tj
T*
(   Phi_0 = h / \( 2 * e \) = \( 6.62607 * 10^-34 J-s \) / \( 2 * 1.60218 * 10^-19 C \) = 2.06783 *) Tj
T*
(   10^-15 Weber \(Tesla-m^2\).) Tj
T*
(   \(Note: The experimental confirmation of the factor of '2' in the denominator was historical) Tj
T*
(   proof that charge carriers are electron PAIRS\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
