(   [Problem Statement]: Calculate the Fermi energy E_F, Fermi velocity v_F, and Fermi temperature T_F for Copper, assuming each Cu atom contributes one free conduction electron. Given: atomic mass M = 63.54 g/mol, density rho = 8.94 g/cm^3, m_e = 9.109 * 10^-31 kg, h = 6.626 * 10^-34 J-s.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Conduction Electron Number Density 'n':) Tj
T*
(   Each atom contributes 1 free electron \(monovalent metal\).) Tj
T*
(   n = \( rho * N_A \) / M = [ \(8940 kg/m^3\) * \(6.022 * 10^23 /mol\) ] / \( 63.54 * 10^-3 kg/mol \).) Tj
T*
(   n = \( 5.38367 * 10^27 \) / \( 63.54 * 10^-3 \) = 8.473 * 10^28 electrons / m^3.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Fermi Energy E_F Calculation:) Tj
T*
(   E_F0 = \( h_bar^2 / \(2 * m_e\) \) * \( 3 * pi^2 * n \)^\(2/3\).) Tj
T*
(   - h_bar = h / \(2 * pi\) = 1.05457 * 10^-34 J-s.) Tj
T*
(   - 3 * pi^2 * n = 3 * \(9.8696\) * \(8.473 * 10^28\) = 2.5088 * 10^30 m^-3.) Tj
T*
(   - \( 3 * pi^2 * n \)^\(2/3\) = \( 2.5088 * 10^30 \)^\(2/3\) = \( 2.5088^\(2/3\) \) * \( 10^20 \) = 1.8465 *) Tj
T*
(   10^20 m^-2.) Tj
T*
(   - h_bar^2 / \(2 * m_e\) = \( 1.05457 * 10^-34 \)^2 / \( 2 * 9.109 * 10^-31 \) = 1.1121 * 10^-68 /) Tj
T*
(   1.8218 * 10^-30 = 6.1044 * 10^-39 J*m^2.) Tj
T*
(   - E_F0 = \( 6.1044 * 10^-39 \) * \( 1.8465 * 10^20 \) = 1.1272 * 10^-18 Joules.) Tj
T*
(   Converting to electron-volts \(1 eV = 1.60218 * 10^-19 J\):) Tj
T*
(   E_F0 = 1.1272 * 10^-18 J / 1.60218 * 10^-19 J/eV = 7.035 eV =~ 7.04 eV.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Fermi Velocity v_F:) Tj
T*
(   v_F = sqrt\( 2 * E_F / m_e \) = sqrt\( 2 * 1.1272 * 10^-18 / 9.109 * 10^-31 \) = sqrt\( 2.4749 *) Tj
T*
(   10^12 \) = 1.573 * 10^6 m/s.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Fermi Temperature T_F:) Tj
T*
(   T_F = E_F / k_B = \( 1.1272 * 10^-18 J \) / \( 1.3806 * 10^-23 J/K \) = 81,645 K =~ 81,650 Kelvin.) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion: E_F = 7.04 eV; v_F = 1.57 * 10^6 m/s; T_F = 81,650 K.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
