(   [Problem Statement]: A semiconductor crystal has an energy band dispersion described by the tight-binding relation: E\(k\) = E0 - 2 * t * cos\(k * a\), where t = 1.2 eV and a = 0.30 nm. Calculate: \(1\) Width of the allowed conduction band, \(2\) Electron group velocity at k = pi / \(2*a\), \(3\) Effective mass m* at the bottom of the band \(k = 0\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Width of Allowed Conduction Band:) Tj
T*
(   The cosine function cos\(ka\) varies between - 1 and + 1.) Tj
T*
(   - Maximum energy \(at k = pi/a\): E_max = E0 - 2*t*\(- 1\) = E0 + 2*t.) Tj
T*
(   - Minimum energy \(at k = 0\): E_min = E0 - 2*t*\(+ 1\) = E0 - 2*t.) Tj
T*
(   - Total Bandwidth: Delta E = E_max - E_min = \(E0 + 2*t\) - \(E0 - 2*t\) = 4 * t.) Tj
T*
(   Given t = 1.2 eV:) Tj
T*
(   Delta E = 4 * \(1.2 eV\) = 4.8 eV.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Group Velocity v_g at k = pi / \(2*a\):) Tj
T*
(   v_g = \(1 / h_bar\) * \(dE / dk\).) Tj
T*
(   dE / dk = d/dk [ E0 - 2*t*cos\(ka\) ] = 2 * t * a * sin\(ka\).) Tj
T*
ET

