(   [Problem Statement]: State and prove Bloch's Theorem for an electron moving in a one-dimensional periodic crystal potential V\(x\) = V\(x + a\). Explain the properties of Bloch wave functions.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Principle Statement:) Tj
T*
(   Bloch's Theorem \(Felix Bloch, 1928\) states that the eigenfunctions of the one-electron) Tj
T*
(   Schrodinger equation for a periodic potential) Tj
T*
(   V\(x\) = V\(x + a\) have the form of a plane wave modulated by a periodic function u_k\(x\) that) Tj
T*
(   possesses the identical translational periodicity of the crystal lattice:) Tj
T*
(   psi_k\(x\) = e^\(i * k * x\) * u_k\(x\), where u_k\(x + a\) = u_k\(x\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Proof using Translation Operator:) Tj
T*
(   Let the crystal Hamiltonian be H_hat = - \(h_bar^2 / 2m\) * \(d^2/dx^2\) + V\(x\).) Tj
T*
(   Since V\(x + a\) = V\(x\), the Hamiltonian commutes with the lattice translation operator T_hat_a) Tj
T*
(   \(which shifts coordinates by lattice vector a\):) Tj
T*
(   T_hat_a * psi\(x\) = psi\(x + a\).) Tj
T*
(   Since [ H_hat, T_hat_a ] = 0, they possess a common set of simultaneous eigenfunctions.) Tj
T*
(   Let lambda be the eigenvalue of T_hat_a:) Tj
T*
(   T_hat_a * psi\(x\) = psi\(x + a\) = lambda * psi\(x\).) Tj
T*
(   Now consider a 1D ring of N lattice sites with periodic Born-von Karman boundary condition) Tj
T*
(   psi\(x + N*a\) = psi\(x\):) Tj
T*
(   \(T_hat_a\)^N * psi\(x\) = psi\(x + N*a\) = lambda^N * psi\(x\) = psi\(x\) => lambda^N = 1.) Tj
T*
(   Therefore: lambda = e^\( i * 2*pi * n / N \) = e^\( i * k * a \), where k = 2*pi*n / \(N*a\).) Tj
T*
(   Thus: psi\(x + a\) = e^\( i * k * a \) * psi\(x\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Form of Wave Function:) Tj
T*
(   Define u_k\(x\) = e^\(- i * k * x\) * psi\(x\).) Tj
T*
(   Then u_k\(x + a\) = e^\(- i * k * \(x + a\)\) * psi\(x + a\) = e^\(- i * k * x\) * e^\(- i * k * a\) * [) Tj
T*
(   e^\(i * k * a\) * psi\(x\) ] = e^\(- i * k * x\) * psi\(x\) = u_k\(x\).) Tj
T*
(   Rearranging yields: psi_k\(x\) = e^\(i * k * x\) * u_k\(x\). \(Q.E.D.\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
