(   The London brothers phenomenologically described electrodynamics of superconductors by dividing) Tj
T*
(   electrons into normal electrons and superconducting electrons \(density n_s\).) Tj
T*
(   - Acceleration without resistance: Superconducting electrons move without friction under) Tj
T*
(   electric field E:) Tj
T*
(   m * \(dv_s / dt\) = - e * E.) Tj
T*
(   Current density J_s = - n_s * e * v_s => dJ_s / dt = - n_s * e * \(dv_s / dt\) = - n_s * e * \( -) Tj
T*
(   e * E / m \).) Tj
T*
(   First London Equation: dJ_s / dt = \( n_s * e^2 / m \) * E. \(Explains zero electrical) Tj
T*
(   resistance\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Second London Equation \(Meissner Effect\):) Tj
T*
(   Taking the curl of both sides of the First London Equation:) Tj
T*
(   Curl\( dJ_s / dt \) = \( n_s * e^2 / m \) * Curl\(E\).) Tj
T*
(   Using Faraday's Law Curl\(E\) = - dB/dt:) Tj
T*
(   d/dt [ Curl\(J_s\) + \( n_s * e^2 / m \) * B ] = 0.) Tj
T*
(   To enforce the Meissner effect \(B = 0 in static state\), London postulated that the bracketed) Tj
T*
(   quantity is not merely constant, but IDENTICALLY ZERO:) Tj
T*
(   Second London Equation: Curl\(J_s\) = - \( n_s * e^2 / m \) * B.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Derivation of London Penetration Depth lambda_L:) Tj
T*
(   By Maxwell's Ampere law \(neglecting displacement current for steady fields\): Curl\(B\) = mu_0 *) Tj
T*
(   J_s.) Tj
T*
(   Taking the curl of both sides: Curl\(Curl\(B\)\) = mu_0 * Curl\(J_s\).) Tj
T*
(   Using vector identity Curl\(Curl\(B\)\) = Grad\(Div B\) - Del^2\(B\), and Gauss's law Div\(B\) = 0:) Tj
T*
(   - Del^2\(B\) = mu_0 * [ - \( n_s * e^2 / m \) * B ].) Tj
T*
(   Del^2\(B\) = \( mu_0 * n_s * e^2 / m \) * B.) Tj
T*
(   Defining London Penetration Depth: lambda_L = sqrt\( m / \( mu_0 * n_s * e^2 \) \):) Tj
T*
(   Del^2\(B\) = B / \(lambda_L^2\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Exponential Field Decay at Surface:) Tj
T*
(   For a semi-infinite superconductor occupying x > 0 with external field B0 applied at surface x) Tj
T*
(   = 0:) Tj
T*
(   d^2B / dx^2 = B / lambda_L^2 => B\(x\) = B0 * exp\( - x / lambda_L \).) Tj
T*
(   Physical significance: Magnetic field does not vanish discontinuously at the surface, but) Tj
T*
(   decays exponentially over skin depth lambda_L \(~ 50 nm\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
