(   [Problem Statement]: A superconducting material has a London penetration depth of lambda_L\(0\) = 40 nm at T = 0 K and a critical temperature T_c = 9.0 K. Using Gorter-Casimir two-fluid model relation lambda_L\(T\) = lambda_L\(0\) / sqrt\(1 - \(T/T_c\)^4\), compute the penetration depth at T = 4.5 K and T = 8.5 K.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Gorter-Casimir Temperature Dependence of Penetration Depth:) Tj
T*
(   lambda_L\(T\) = lambda_L\(0\) * [ 1 - \( T / T_c \)^4 ]^\(- 1/2\).) Tj
T*
(   Given lambda_L\(0\) = 40.0 nm, T_c = 9.0 K.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Penetration Depth at T = 4.5 K:) Tj
T*
(   T / T_c = 4.5 / 9.0 = 0.50.) Tj
T*
(   \( T / T_c \)^4 = \(0.50\)^4 = 0.0625.) Tj
T*
(   1 - \( T / T_c \)^4 = 1 - 0.0625 = 0.9375.) Tj
T*
(   sqrt\( 0.9375 \) = 0.96825.) Tj
T*
(   lambda_L\(4.5 K\) = 40.0 nm / 0.96825 = 41.31 nm.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Penetration Depth at T = 8.5 K:) Tj
T*
(   T / T_c = 8.5 / 9.0 = 0.94444.) Tj
T*
