(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Powder Method \(Debye-Scherrer Technique\) of X-ray crystal structure analysis. Describe the experimental setup, formation of diffraction cones, and how lattice parameters are indexed.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Principle of the Powder Method:) Tj
T*
(   Developed by Peter Debye and Paul Scherrer \(1916\) and independently by A.W. Hull.) Tj
T*
(   A finely powdered polycrystalline sample containing millions of tiny microscopic crystallites) Tj
T*
(   randomly oriented in all possible spatial directions) Tj
T*
(   is irradiated by a collimated beam of monochromatic X-rays of known wavelength lambda.) Tj
T*
(   Because all orientations are present simultaneously, for EVERY set of crystal planes \(hkl\) with) Tj
T*
(   spacing d_hkl, some crystallites will be) Tj
T*
(   oriented at the exact Bragg glancing angle theta: 2 * d * sin\(theta\) = lambda.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Formation of Diffraction Cones:) Tj
T*
(   The reflected rays from all crystallites satisfying Bragg's condition for a given \(hkl\) plane) Tj
T*
(   form a continuous cone of diffracted radiation) Tj
T*
(   with semi-vertical apex angle 2*theta centered along the incident beam axis.) Tj
T*
(   A cylindrical strip of photographic film \(or modern curved position-sensitive detector\) placed) Tj
T*
(   coaxially around the sample intercepts these cones,) Tj
T*
(   recording pairs of circular arc lines symmetrical about the exit hole.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Indexing and Lattice Parameter Determination:) Tj
T*
(   - Measure distance S between symmetrical arc pairs on the film of radius R: S = \( 4 * theta \) *) Tj
T*
(   R \(where theta is in radians\).) Tj
T*
(   - Therefore: theta = S / \( 4 * R \).) Tj
T*
(   - Compute interplanar spacing d from Bragg's law: d = lambda / \( 2 * sin\(theta\) \).) Tj
T*
(   - For a cubic lattice: 1 / d^2 = \( h^2 + k^2 + l^2 \) / a^2.) Tj
T*
(   - Ratio of \(1/d^2\) values yields ratios of \(h^2 + k^2 + l^2\):) Tj
T*
(   * Simple Cubic: 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, ...) Tj
T*
(   * Body-Centered Cubic \(h+k+l = even\): 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, ...) Tj
T*
(   * Face-Centered Cubic \(all odd/even\): 3, 4, 8, 11, 12, 16, 19, 20, ...) Tj
T*
(   - Lattice constant 'a' is then computed with extreme precision.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
