T*
(   2. Case Study: Sodium \(Na, Metal, Z = 11\):) Tj
T*
(   - Electron configuration: 1s^2 2s^2 2p^6 3s^1.) Tj
T*
(   - The completely filled 1s, 2s, 2p core levels remain tightly bound with negligible overlap) Tj
T*
(   \(narrow core bands\).) Tj
T*
(   - The outermost 3s orbital has 1 valence electron per atom, but can hold 2 electrons per atom) Tj
T*
(   \(spin up/down\).) Tj
T*
(   - Thus, for N sodium atoms, the 3s band contains 2*N available quantum states but only N) Tj
T*
(   electrons.) Tj
T*
(   - The 3s conduction band is EXACTLY HALF-FILLED. Plentiful empty states exist immediately above) Tj
T*
(   the Fermi energy.) Tj
T*
