(   3. Case Study: Carbon in Diamond \(Insulator, Z = 6\):) Tj
T*
(   - Isolated configuration: 1s^2 2s^2 2p^2 \(4 valence electrons: two 2s, two 2p\).) Tj
T*
(   - In diamond tetrahedral bonding, 2s and three 2p orbitals hybridize into four equivalent sp^3) Tj
T*
(   hybrid orbitals per atom.) Tj
T*
(   - Upon crystal formation, sp^3 orbitals split into: 4*N bonding states \(Valence Band\) and 4*N) Tj
T*
(   antibonding states \(Conduction Band\).) Tj
T*
(   - All 4*N valence electrons completely fill the lower bonding valence band.) Tj
T*
